Close a card without doing it. --reason is required: obsolete, duplicate
or wontfix. A duplicate must name the surviving card with --dup. Dropping a
story with open children needs --cascade, which drops them too with the same
reason and releases their claims. A dropped story is not folded. Decisions are
dropped with 'lorvik decisions reject' or 'revoke'.

Examples:
  lorvik drop 42 --reason wontfix -m "out of scope for v1"
  lorvik drop 43 --reason duplicate --dup 42
  lorvik drop 20 --reason wontfix --cascade -m "abandoned"

Usage
  lorvik drop <number> [flags]

Flags
      --cascade          Drop a story's open children along with it
      --dup int          Surviving card number when the reason is duplicate
  -h, --help             help for drop
  -m, --message string   Short note recorded on the event
      --reason string    obsolete, duplicate or wontfix (required)

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)
